WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:00.000
[Music]

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:06.560
[Narrator:] By air, by land, and by
sea. All routes lead to this southern city.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:11.380
Beautiful scenery and sunny skies
attract many additional residents each year.

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:15.680
Unfortunately, this climate is also
ideal for one of man's worst enemies:

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:21.560
the aedes aegypti mosquito, carrier of dengue and yellow fever.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:02:35.600
[Music]

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:39.780
To combat this menace to the city,
an officer of the United States Public Health Service

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:42.500
cooperated with the local health department.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:47.620
One of the first steps in the campaign
was to discover permanent mosquito breeding places

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:54.860
such as old cisterns, basins, shallow wells, fire barrels, and numerous other containers capable of holding water.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:03:00.100
Health officials have constantly warned
the people of these dangerous conditions,

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:04.959
and of the way mosquitoes spread to smaller receptacles.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:12.800
After a period devoted to study and
survey, the extent of breeding of the dengue

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:15.200
and yellow fever mosquito was determined.

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:19.400
A special meeting of health officials
set in motion the anti-mosquito campaign.

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:26.260
It was decided that a concerted effort
would be necessary, enlisting the aid of every source of publicity

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:31.800
together with the organized individual
efforts of all the people.

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:44.420
With the health of an entire city
in jeopardy, the mayor promptly issued a proclamation

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:46.900
regarding the urgency of the situation,

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:53.640
and asked that everyone participate in eliminating the dengue-yellow fever mosquito.

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:03.940
Newspapers proved particularly valuable
in awakening the public to an understanding

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:07.100
of their common danger and mutual dependence.

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:20.539
Officials of civic organizations assisted
to help officers in recruiting leaders

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:25.940
and obtaining cooperation from the public through knowledge, rather than action and force by law.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:44.840
Theaters exhibited short films showing methods of control of the dengue and yellow fever mosquito: Aedes Aegypti.

00:05:00.140 --> 00:05:05.600
Teamwork was stimulated in schools
as a direct result of the educational program,

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:10.060
which included the showing of motion pictures on mosquitoes, their life habits,

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:11.520
and various methods of control.

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:18.660
Children are impressed by this method of presentation.

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:23.860
Such knowledge acquired by these citizens
of tomorrow, will be of great influence

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:30.020
in the building of healthy, prosperous communities of tomorrow.

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:40.180
Progress of the campaign was broadcast
daily by local radio stations.

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:43.700
This method was most effective in
reaching the housewife,

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:46.400
the self-appointed guardian of the family welfare,

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:52.740
whose cooperation is vital to the
success of any health campaign.

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:58.260
Instructions and educational material
were supplied to the Boy Scouts,

00:05:58.260 --> 00:06:03.330
since they had volunteered to inspect
homes and tell the people about the hazards of the city.

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:08.760
Districts were set up based on geography
and population.

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:16.400
As an additional incentive for action, it was decided to give a V merit award to cooperating residents.

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:23.140
Pamphlets on the aedes aegypti mosquito were made available for distribution to every home,

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:26.740
together with an instruction sheet
showing methods of destroying

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:31.820
their breeding places and posters urging definite action.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:41.840
Newspaper publicity gave the necessary
day-by-day stimulus for a successful campaign.

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:50.860
Schoolchildren were eager to take
part in the mosquito control program,

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:54.230
since they had been so thoroughly informed of its importance.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:59.440
Teachers emphasized the necessity
of the campaign by personally distributing

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:04.580
literature for the children to take home.

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:13.660
Parents were interested and realized the need for eliminating the dengue and yellow fever mosquito.

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:19.220
They welcomed instructions on how to get rid of mosquitoes in and around their home.

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:26.400
A call to arms found the Boy Scouts
prepared and anxious to undertake their duty.

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:33.880
After being instructed by their leader, they started on their way to distribute pamphlets and inspect premises.

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:44.220
The Scouts greeted housewives in their usual polite manner

00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:47.520
and consequently received cooperation and assistance.

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:51.620
Each scout had received instructions
about possible breeding places

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:55.080
and was determined to make a thorough inspection of each home.

00:07:55.080 --> 00:08:00.800
This attitude often stimulated the
housewife's concern and careful observation.

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:08.960
If it holds water, it will hold mosquito
larvae.

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:18.480
Another home, another scout, and another
housewife.

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:28.420
The water in this container is fresh...there are no larvae here but they could develop within a few days.

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:33.000
But let's look in other containers.

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:42.680
Ah, here they are! Who would imagine so many larvae in such a small piece of pottery?

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:54.540
Any container capable of catching
water is a potential mosquito breeding place

00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:58.960
and should be immediately destroyed
or emptied and turned bottoms up.

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:10.940
A careful search is necessary to find the hidden containers which provide permanent breeding places.

00:09:12.140 --> 00:09:17.820
Larvae become mosquitoes. Mosquitoes
carry disease.

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:30.720
Inside or outside, it makes no difference.

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:38.020
Man-made containers, small and large,
harbor aedes aegypti mosquito larvae.

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:55.860
Discarded containers of this type should always be given to salvage and garbage collectors without delay.

00:09:56.120 --> 00:10:00.840
Constant protection of the family
health demands constant vigilance.

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:14.180
All drinking pans should be emptied
and washed at least twice a week.

00:10:14.360 --> 00:10:17.619
Mosquitoes breed continually and are
most prolific,

00:10:17.620 --> 00:10:22.880
one mosquito being able to lay hundreds
of eggs within a single day.

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:37.080
After each home had been thoroughly
inspected, the cooperative housewife was given a merit award.

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:40.680
Display of this award was evidence
of her intention to continue

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:45.240
keeping her home free from dengue and yellow fever mosquitoes.

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:57.480
Informative articles published in the newspapers were effective in making housewives

00:10:57.500 --> 00:10:59.320
conscious of mosquito-breeding places.

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:05.660
The effect of this information was often instantaneous.

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:12.660
Horrified? No wonder. Such a small
plant and all those wiggle tails in the water.

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:32.660
All water plant receptacles in the
home should be emptied and scrubbed twice a week.

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:50.620
The stems of the plant should be carefully
rinsed to remove any remaining mosquito larvae.

00:11:50.860 --> 00:11:55.220
A simple operation indeed, but only
by such precautions can any home

00:11:55.420 --> 00:12:00.000
be kept free of the disease-carrying aedes aegypti mosquito.

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:22.440
Since most water plants grow well
in soil, it was recommended that where possible

00:12:22.449 --> 00:12:23.899
the change be made.

00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:28.200
Potted plants never breed mosquitoes.

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:42.720
Girl Scouts were enlisted in the all-out
campaign.

00:12:42.940 --> 00:12:47.940
They discovered and destroyed numerous
breeding places including those in cemeteries.

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:54.980
In order to stimulate greater interest
in the collection and destruction of mosquito larvae.

00:12:55.470 --> 00:12:59.670
schoolchildren were encouraged to
collect the wiggle tails and feed them to minnows.

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:06.480
Such action also emphasized the importance of fish as a protective measure.

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:17.120
Minnows like these, when placed in
garden pools and similar places, eat mosquito larvae.

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:25.300
Every section of the city was thoroughly inspected.

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:29.460
Vacant lots were found with accumulations
of refuse.

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:37.520
The scouts punched holes in containers
to make sure they would never again be capable

00:13:37.520 --> 00:13:40.540
of holding water and mosquito larvae.

00:13:41.140 --> 00:13:45.199
Community cooperation is essential
in all health education programs,

00:13:45.200 --> 00:13:50.040
since clean-up in one area contributes
to the welfare of the entire community.

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:57.540
Mosquito larvae are often found in
unsuspected places,

00:13:57.600 --> 00:14:00.459
such as old discarded tires containing water.

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:04.360
There's just about one efficient way
to get water out of these tires.

00:14:08.440 --> 00:14:09.840
And this is it.

00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:23.940
After the water is removed from such tires, they should be stored in dry, sheltered locations until salvaged.

00:14:26.340 --> 00:14:31.680
This man, by cooperating in the campaign, helps protect the health of his family and neighbors,

00:14:32.440 --> 00:14:37.179
thereby receiving the merit award.

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:45.720
Thousands of rusty, damaged containers were promptly removed from homes by the city sanitary department.

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:50.840
This is one of the most effective methods for the permanent elimination of mosquito-breeding places.

00:14:53.440 --> 00:15:00.300
A brief survey of the huge collection
was made by health and sanitary officials before salvaging or destruction.

00:15:06.720 --> 00:15:10.080
Posters were displayed throughout
the city to keep the public

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:12.400
ever mindful of the mosquito menace.

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:24.720
Store owners contributed window space
for unusual exhibits, conveying to the public

00:15:24.720 --> 00:15:27.119
the danger of mosquito breeding.

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:32.399
Various methods of aedes aegypti control
were presented.

00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:39.780
The display of live mosquitoes and
larvae attracted the attention of thousands of people.

00:15:47.320 --> 00:15:52.500
The larvae-eating minnows impress
many spectators as being an effective way

00:15:52.500 --> 00:15:54.220
to combat the mosquito hazard.

00:15:57.100 --> 00:16:02.180
The aroused public attitude assured the success of the anti-mosquito campaign.

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:21.480
[Music]

00:16:24.440 --> 00:16:29.000
You have just observed how one city
awakened to the potential danger of uncontrolled

00:16:29.320 --> 00:16:32.220
dengue and yellow fever mosquito breeding

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:35.280
and cooperated in an urgent community project.

00:16:35.960 --> 00:16:38.620
By organizing the entire population of the city,

00:16:38.920 --> 00:16:43.460
immediate results were obtained and
citizens continued the control program

00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:47.440
to ensure permanent freedom from dengue and yellow fever.

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:56.680
Every community has a wealth of resource,
but its greatest resource is its people.

00:16:57.140 --> 00:17:00.580
Capable leaders can develop the power and ability of the people

00:17:00.860 --> 00:17:03.820
to assure a victorious mosquito-control program.

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:06.700
It's up to you!

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:16.420
[Music]

